; The one shift whose left operand is UNSIGNED. It is computed on a u64 holding
; the 32-bit pattern, so `>>` is the logical shift the operator wants; done on
; `int` it would be arithmetic and every negative input would answer wrong.
function jsnum_unsigned_right_shift(x: u64, y: u64) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns u64 linked


