; Exponentiate (tc39 §6.1.6.1.3). ★★★ THE ONE OPERATOR IN THIS FILE THAT DOES
; NOT AGREE WITH THE REFERENCE TO THE BIT, and the disagreement is bounded,
; measured and gated rather than described.
;
; TWO CAUSES, and the first is the one a reader will not expect. **Go's
; `math.Pow` is not libm's `pow`** — it is a Go implementation over Frexp / Log /
; Exp / Sqrt / Ldexp with its own special cases (`y == 0.5` becomes `Sqrt`, an
; integer exponent becomes repeated squaring), so the two round differently.
; Measured by tests/arithcheck.sh over 20 000 pairs, and the first draft of this
; note got the MAGNITUDE wrong by inheriting it from upstream's comment instead
; of reading the instrument: **3 867 lines differ — 2 815 of them a NaN PAYLOAD
; and 1 052 a mantissa, the worst gap 113 ULP (`0.2 ** 254` and its neighbours),
; and no other operator differs on any line.** ★What DOES agree on every line, in
; both directions, is the CATEGORY: NaN-ness, an infinity and its sign, the sign
; of a finite answer, and a zero. That is the half a port owes, and it is what
; the instrument pins. The second cause is upstream's own: for an integer base
; and exponent whose result exceeds 53 bits it routes through `big.Int.Exp`,
; because `math.Pow` is several ULPs off there too — and its comment says the
; spec calls this value "implementation-approximated", so even that answer is not
; THE answer.
;
; ★★★ WHY THIS IS ACCEPTED RATHER THAN CLOSED, with the price named. Closing it
; means porting `math.Pow`, `math.Exp` and `math.Log` — roughly 250 lines of
; coefficient-table numerics whose only reader is this operator. What that would
; buy, swept over both corpora with comments stripped: **1 021 enum bodies, of
; which exactly ONE contains `**` at all** (`constEnums.ts`'s `PQ = E ** 2`,
; where E is 1, and 1 ** 2 is exact in any implementation). So the input that
; separates the two is not merely absent from the corpus — it is absent by a
; margin of fifty-three bits.
;
; ★★ AND THE ACCEPTANCE IS A GATE, NOT A SILENCE. arithcheck.sh compares this
; column by CATEGORY exactly and by mantissa against a bound of 512 ULP, and
; prints the count and the worst gap; a category flip, a gap past the bound, or
; any drift at all in the other twelve operators turns it red. ★The reader that
; closes it is a fixture whose enum value is a non-exact power — write one and
; the numerics have to be built. ★The reader that makes it observable is a fixture
; someone writes for it, and then this arm has to be built — a big-integer
; power, which is why it was not built speculatively.
function jsnum_exponentiate(base_bits: u64, exponent_bits: u64) @deep true returns u64 linked


















